 field\n     - `OrderController.kt` - added cancel endpoint\n     - `OrderRepository.kt` - not modified (no need for new methods)\n     - `ShipmentRepository.kt` - added findByOrderId helper\n     - `ShipmentController.kt` - added order status validation\n     - `ApiError.kt` - added new error codes\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **Order.kt**: Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order data class with default ACTIVE status ✓\n- **OrderController.kt**: Added dependency on shipmentRepository, added cancel endpoint with proper logic for all cases ✓\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Added findByOrderId method to support cascade lookup ✓\n- **ShipmentController.kt**: Added orderRepository dependency and validation in create to reject shipments for cancelled orders ✓\n- **ApiError.kt**: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS error codes ✓\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Added 7 new comprehensive tests covering all cancel scenarios ✓\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Added 4 new tests covering shipment creation with cancelled orders and baseline behavior ✓\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All requirements are met and all edge cases are tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that transitions active orders to cancelled status, handles edge cases (already cancelled, shipments confirmed, non-existent orders), and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged:\n- **Order.kt** - Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order data class\n- **OrderController.kt** - Added cancel endpoint implementing all business logic and cascading shipment updates\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added findByOrderId method to query shipments by order\n- **ShipmentController.kt** - Added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- **ApiError.kt** - Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS error codes\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 7 comprehensive tests for cancel endpoint (status transitions, idempotency, rejections, cascading)\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 4 tests for shipment creation validation with cancelled orders\n\nTests:\n- \"creates an order with ACTIVE status by default\" - Verifies new orders default to ACTIVE\n- \"cancels an active order and returns 200\" - Verifies successful cancellation with status change\n- \"cancelling a non-existent order returns 404 with error envelope\" - Verifies 404 for missing orders\n- \"cancelling an already cancelled order is idempotent\" - Verifies repeated cancel succeeds (AC 5)\n- \"cancelling an order with confirmed shipment is rejected with 409\" - Verifies rejection and state preservation (AC 5)\n- \"cancelling an order cancels all its created shipments\" - Verifies cascade to CREATED shipments (AC 3)\n- \"allows creating shipment for non-existent order\" - Verifies baseline behavior preserved\n- \"rejects creating shipment for cancelled order with 409\" - Verifies rejection with ORDER_CANCELLED (AC 5)\n\nVerification: \n- Command: `./mvnw test`\n- Result: BUILD SUCCESS - Tests run: 21, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\n- All existing tests continue to pass; new tests validate all acceptance criteria\n\nNot done: None. All acceptance criteria implemented and verified.","ttft_ms":4567,"type":"result","duration_ms":235288,"uuid":"f0fb7235-e767-46c1-bbda-36961be0f808","ttft_stream_ms":1232,"time_to_request_ms":22,"first_content_frame_ms":1498,"queued_turn_count":0}

